{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>The fifth time</b><br>And comely. Like יפה, like לא נאוה לכסיל תענוג, לא יאות לו. And the nun [in ונאוה] is for the nifal pattern, like וכל נעשה במרחשת." "<b>The second time</b><br>[And she returned and said to the maidens] who are the daughters of Jerusalem: If I am dark compared to you — I am like the tents of Kedar, upon which the sun [beats constantly upon their tents] — I am comely and beautiful of form like the curtains of Solomon the king. And do not suppose of me that I was born with this darkness; rather it is incidental and passing, and its cause is the sun that struck me outdoors, for my mother's sons made strife with me and set me as a guard; and before this, I did not even guard my own vineyard." "<b>The third time</b><br>שחורה אני (ונאוה). Afterward I went down to Egypt, even though [I] was comely, for I adhered to the rest of the commandments."], :book :song-of-songs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {1 "Bracketed opening phrase [וחזרה ואמרה לעלמות] appears incomplete in the Hebrew; translated as found. The word שיכם is rendered hyper-literally 'that beats upon them'; its form is unusual and possibly corrupt.", 2 "The bracketed ש in [ש]הייתי is supplied editorially in the source."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra's commentary on the Canticles" "http://beta.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH002030344/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:43:50.035527115Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}